# Shell scripts must arrive with LF, whatever the checkout platform does by
# default. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true otherwise writes CRLF, and
# bash then reads `set -euo pipefail\r` and refuses:
#
#     tests/safety_honesty.sh: line 4: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# This is a checkout attribute, not a content change: every tracked .sh blob in
# this repository is already pure LF, so nothing preserved here is rewritten.
*.sh text eol=lf
